 "notes": "Generated-row sibling (#4507) of genapp-lgipol01: GenApp's inquire-policy front end (LGIPOL01, LINKed with the 32500-byte LGCMAREA COMMAREA) LINKs LGIPDB01 in the same task (LGSTSQ too, its error logger) on the generated CUSTOMER, POLICY and ENDOWMENT / HOUSE / MOTOR / COMMERCIAL rows of genapp-lgipdb01-generated (same generate block, seed 4507: identity policy numbers 1000001..1000012, FKs POLICY->CUSTOMER and type->POLICY, NULLs and boundary values), not GenApp's INSERTs. The 32 generated requests are genapp-lgipdb01-generated's (found, wrong customer, policy of another type, 02ICOM by policy, 03ICOM Cust_Cursor, 05ICOM Zip_Cursor, unknown request ids), each now entering through the front end; the stated no-commarea scenario (EIBCALEN 0: LGSTSQ, ABEND LGCA) is the front end's own. A change to the generator's draw moves which policies exist: the E2E test in tests/cobol_mainframe/test_equivalence_db2_rows.py fails the case then. Not generated, as in genapp-lgipdb01-generated: an endowment inquiry on policy 1000010 (empty PADDINGDATA, a zero-length reference modification, oracle_assumptions.md X8); the error paths on the SELECT, OPEN and CLOSE (genapp-lgipdb01's). WRITE-ERROR-MESSAGE's IF EIBCALEN > 0 is never true (the paragraph is PERFORMed only when EIBCALEN is zero): dead in practice. Derived from the CICS General Insurance Application (GenApp, github.com/cicsdev/cics-genapp; (C) Copyright IBM Corp. 2011, 2020), licensed under the Eclipse Public License 2.0: LICENSE here is the corpus's own, NOTICE names the source and what was derived.",
